   210	## 2. What the project is (and the protagonist)
   211	
   212	The reproduction target is **MODQN**: a value-based multi-objective DQN that, for
   213	each user each step, selects a serving beam to jointly optimize **throughput**,
   214	**handover cost**, and **load balance**. The repo reproduces its environment
   215	(orbit / beam / channel / step semantics), training, evaluation, and sweep
   216	surfaces, and freezes that as a **disclosed comparison baseline**.
   217	
   218	The research goal layered on top is **Multi-Catfish**: a *training-strategy*
   219	enhancement that adds one or more "catfish" challenger learners to stir the main
   220	learner out of lazy/homogeneous policies (an analogy to the "catfish effect").
   221	Multi-Catfish is the **named protagonist** of the research arc. Everything else
   222	(coordination decoders, per-objective wiring, specific ablation arms) is internal
   223	machinery of particular *attempts* to realize Multi-Catfish — not the headline.
   224	
   225	**Claim ceiling everywhere in this repo: READINESS-ONLY.** Code compiling, tests
   226	passing, and a mechanical verdict label are *computations*, not an effectiveness
   227	PASS. A real "beats baseline" claim requires a matched pilot with seed-aggregated
   228	neutral-metric Pareto dominance + an independent adversarial review + sign-off.
