   330	## 6. For future readers / agents: do NOT re-propose these
   331	
   332	Every one of these has been tried in this repo and produced a structural negative.
   333	Proposing them again wastes effort (an external deep-research report did exactly
   334	this because it could not see this ledger):
   335	
   336	- **Value-DQN upgrades on the same axis:** Double / Dueling / Prioritized Replay /
   337	  Rainbow / NoisyNet — all keep per-user `argmax` on shared Q. **QMIX (a stronger
   338	  mixer than dueling) already failed (#5).** These will collapse identically.
   339	- **Action masking** (#7), **hard capacity caps / "make it harder"** (#9, Trap B),
   340	  **reward re-scaling / re-weighting / PopArt** (#11 and others — collapse is
   341	  reward-optimal regardless of weights), **adding co-channel interference** (#15,
   342	  #16, Trap A — it *rewards* collapse).
   343	- **"Be more faithful to the paper"** — already exhausted (#1); the issue is not
   344	  fidelity.
   345	
   346	What is **genuinely untried** (low probability of breaking collapse, but honest
   347	candidates for a *scoped-thesis methodology* rather than a beats-baseline claim):
   348	recurrent / partial-observability (DRQN) models; preference-conditioned MORL
   349	(Envelope-Q / GPI). Adopt regardless: **rliable** statistics (probability of
   350	improvement, IQM, stratified bootstrap CI) and **dual-board** reporting (frozen
   351	baseline env vs. an explicitly-disclosed stress regime).
