/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/CONTROL-LAW-CEILING-2026-09-10.md:23:SEALED headroom combines more delivered bits with lower energy. Under STRICT, energy is nearly flat and the gain is predominantly increased delivered bits; this distinction survives the provisioning repair.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/CONTROL-LAW-CEILING-2026-09-10.md:155:The panel is `V025_PROBE_R2/world/1` and `/2`, steps 0–3, 100 users per anchor, one-sided half-power angle 1.66°. For each rule the fixed assignment is exactly that rule's correctly paired `J_from_first` commit. Thus SEALED and STRICT are each evaluated on the configuration their own current pipeline commits; assignments never change within a C1/C2 pair.
