/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/ABLATION-SURVIVAL-2026-09-10.md:35:1. **Raw-context direct head, fixed shared reference: `S=D(Z,a0,A,a_A)`.** C1 and C2 disappear from ranking and proposal generation. Their neutral substitutions change unused head parameters but cannot change committed configurations through the policy. Calling raw Q1/Q2 fields “route features” does not restore source effects. C3 can affect ranking if its source now trains `D`, but it has become joint-objective supervision. This is the relevant trap in the measured DIRECT implementation: its Q1 feature bank uses feature moments and fixed random weights, and DIRECT predicts from that feature matrix without consuming the separately fitted additive head. [compare_target_parametrisations.py:441](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/scripts/compare_target_parametrisations.py:441), [compare_target_parametrisations.py:1010](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/scripts/compare_target_parametrisations.py:1010), [compare_target_parametrisations.py:1030](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/scripts/compare_target_parametrisations.py:1030).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/ABLATION-SURVIVAL-2026-09-10.md:37:2. **Replace only the immediate pair: `S=D+sum_i v_i`.** C2 retains its original continuation source and direct ranking path. C1 is still disconnected at a fixed reference unless another path is added. C3's training target is still changed from Ψ to J. Adding `sum_i u_i` as well would restore C1 mechanically, but count unilateral immediate value again; that is not the stated replacement.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/ABLATION-SURVIVAL-2026-09-10.md:39:3. **C1/C2 survive only through arm-specific proposal and repair.** Each arm must actually compute `a0_r=repair(argmax(q1_r+q2_r))` with its own retained heads. Neutral training can then alter BASE, the changed-user set/context, BASE tie preference, reference-relative guard inputs and timeout fallback. Those are real paths to a different commit. Identical authenticated catalogues must still be maintained at matched anchors; silently changing candidate coverage would introduce another intervention. If `sum_i v_i` remains in the score, C2 additionally retains its ranking path. If it is removed, C2 has only the proposal path and its continuation value no longer directly scores candidates. The underlying reference, matching and fallback requirements are [contract §A3–A4:8](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:8), [contract §F2:39](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:39).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/ABLATION-SURVIVAL-2026-09-10.md:43:4. **Learned route outputs become direct-head inputs.** A new `D` could consume pooled, paired predictions `q1_r(selected/reference)` and `q2_r(selected/reference)` alongside the physical set context. Neutral C1/C2 training would change those activations and could change ranking, even with a fixed reference. They must be the current arm's outputs; precomputing FULL's predictions for all arms removes this intervention. If preserving route-local training, direct-loss gradients must not retrain Q1/Q2 through a different supervision path. C3 can train `D` on J, but that still changes C3's specified source. This input wiring is absent from the current invariant tensor and fixed `CoalitionBatch.invariant_states`.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/ABLATION-SURVIVAL-2026-09-10.md:55:| Original C1/C2 used only for proposal/repair in option 3 | **Same literal source-claim meaning remains testable**, if the paths operate. A positive result would concern source-trained proposal/repair/fallback quality. Describing it as an additive scoring contribution would be a different claim. |
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/ABLATION-SURVIVAL-2026-09-10.md:60:“Remains testable” is not “remains true”: no design analysis establishes improved pooled EE. Nor does a live route establish FULL > each DROP > ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL. The positive conjunction and ordering require their own paired pooled-efficiency results; direct ranking superiority alone settles none of them. §C5 fixes source generator, labels, support, strata, overlap, weights and optimization dose, and requires neutral-head updates and deployment participation. Those identities cannot be inferred from retained head names. [contract §C5:23](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:23), [learner.py:487](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:487).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/ABLATION-SURVIVAL-2026-09-10.md:74:Train `H_phi` directly against J on declared development data, then hold its parameters and training provenance identical across all five learned arms within a lineage. Preserve Q1/Q2/Ψ training and their neutral sources; do not backpropagate the new loss into them. Declare the readout's training support; training only on informative-head inputs leaves a distribution-shift risk for neutral-head deployment, although the source contrast remains defined. Inference must use each arm's actual outputs, never a substituted informative copy. `D(empty)=0`; singleton direct values are allowed to be nonzero. Q2's continuation remains outside the immediate joint predictor, so no horizon or immediate/continuation accounting is changed. This is a proposed formulation, not existing code.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/ABLATION-SURVIVAL-2026-09-10.md:76:C1 then enters `H_phi` through `u_i`, C3 through `p`, and C2 through `sum v_i`; proposal/repair can remain additional paths. A readout can still learn to ignore an input, or learn compensating dependencies, so actual decision sensitivity and positive source marginals remain empirical requirements. Retaining inputs alone proves neither.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/ABLATION-SURVIVAL-2026-09-10.md:78:The cost is an additional learned component and joint-label training source, a new input/target/checkpoint interface, support for singleton direct predictions, and new deployment evidence. ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL would be neutral for the **three original routes** while still containing informative common readout training. Thus the same literal source-benefit sentence is conditional on that shared predictor; it cannot describe an unchanged three-head system with all learned supervision neutral. The current model inventory and route-local updates contain no such readout. [learner.py:930](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:930), [learner.py:1021](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:1021).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/ABLATION-SURVIVAL-2026-09-10.md:82:Under the fixed project requirements, neither construction is a conforming replacement. §B4 fixes the factor identity, §C1 fixes the Q1/Q2 surrogate, and §C2 fixes residual-only C3 supervision, singleton zero anchoring and the deployed sum. A direct J predictor generally has nonzero singleton and additive-case values, unlike Ψ. Keeping the exact decomposition as a reporting KAT would not make a different deployed score satisfy §C2. [contract §B4:15](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:15), [contract §C1–C2:19](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:19), [learner.py:835](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:835). The observed gain belongs to the measured DIRECT model; its transfer to either source-preserving construction is unverified.
