/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/EVALPATH-2026-09-10.md:104:- **Coalition training rows are mixed.** The primitive builder calls `current.evaluate_many((base, selected))`; BASE is skipped because it is scalar-cached, while the pairwise selected row is dense boundary-0 (`:501-514`). `_coalition_row` then combines scalar reference and scalar-on-miss singleton outcomes with the dense selected outcome (`:910-939`). The joint term’s reference-offset error is the boundary-0 BASE gap; ψ additionally mixes scalar singletons with a dense joint.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/EVALPATH-2026-09-10.md:105:- **Pilot evaluation’s exact boundary-0 selectors are mixed.** `_exact_s0_boundary0` batch-populates candidates but retains scalar BASE, then ranks raw bits (`:1458-1500`). The call into `_s_uni_select` reuses that evaluator (`:1638-1652`); `_s_uni_select` reads BASE/current with `evaluate` and batches candidate neighborhoods (`run_v025_matrix_probe.py:1831-1924`), so its first sweep compares scalar BASE with dense candidates. `_exact_interactions` similarly batches catalogues/singletons and subtracts its cached anchor (`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:1328-1379`); P-a0 uses scalar BASE as that anchor. These can alter S0/S_UNI selection, joint deltas, and ψ—not merely reporting.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/EVALPATH-2026-09-10.md:107:- **Pilot realised reports are path-consistent.** A fresh realised full-grid evaluator batch-populates selected arms before reads (`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:1678-1727`), and reporting singletons are also explicitly batched before the matched decomposition (`:1767-1805`). The reported pooled EE summary uses those realised bits/joules (`:1869-1894`). Selection may already have been corrupted upstream, but the endpoint subtraction itself is not mixed.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/EVALPATH-2026-09-10.md:111:- `diagnose_v025_selector.py` reuses the primitive builder’s scalar-cached BASE, batch-populates configurations/singletons, and labels its results “Exact one-boundary F components” (`diagnose_v025_selector.py:194-224`). Its exact delta/ψ panel and later no-op coalition diagnostic (`:533-570`) can therefore contain the same mixed boundary-policy error.
