/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PARAMETRISATION-COMPARISON-2026-09-10.md:11:Both arms predict the same normalized exact joint objective change, `ΔF/κ`. ADDITIVE fits a shared per-user unilateral-surplus head and a set-conditioned interaction-residual head, then sums them. DIRECT fits one set-conditioned head to `ΔF/κ`. All learned scalars use the same fixed-ReLU random-feature ridge family, split, seed, and grid.
