/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:21:3. **The declared target is unlearnable: unsupported.** The original input representation has effective dimension 12, including two constant slots and two redundant indicators (`results.json`, `slot_audit`). The replacement repairs off-axis angle and adds elevation, reaching effective dimension 14. Its receipt expressly reports no learner or EE result (`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-design-ws/Q1-SCHEMA-V2-2026-09-10.md:1–20`). I found no completed replacement-fit result in `L/.scratch/c1-declared-v2/`. Its performance, and whether a job is still running, are **UNDETERMINED**.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:27:The original 22.99× cancellation argument is unavailable. The opened worker audit derives a mixed-path residual offset `(size−1) × epsilon` and places the alleged cancellation inside its sampled artifact envelope; it explicitly says a corrected decomposition is not determined (`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/PATH-ARTEFACT-CHECKS-2026-09-10.md:11–36`). The feasibility erratum acknowledges this (`C/V025-CONTROLLER-FEASIBILITY-2026-09-10.md:110–126`). An envelope overlap invalidates that particular inference; it does not prove all physical cancellation disappears. **UNDETERMINED:** actual conditioning and achievable decision regret on the repaired, path-consistent target. Settling them requires corresponding labeled receipts and held-out decisions, followed by the specified EE comparison.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:31:**Verified, contract.** The primary experiment is informative versus neutral source training with all heads retained, with three conditional FULL-versus-DROP contrasts. Coordination versus S_UNI is a separate claim. The estimator is pooled `ΣB/ΣE`, paired by arms inside date×learner-seed resamples; the central 95% interval's lower 2.5th percentile must exceed **+0.5% relative**. The primary decision is an intersection–union conjunction (`C/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:21–31`).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:35:**Verified, code and receipts.** The inspected default still defines seed domains with `range(1, 13)`, whereas the amendment requires 16 (`R/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:41–42`; v1.1:14). This establishes a default mismatch, not that a completed formal experiment actually ran twelve seeds: the opened minimal pilot used two seeds, one evaluation world and five anchors (`R/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:7`). The date audit identifies that evaluation world as the single date 2025-11-16 and explicitly reports that the requested paired date-contrast SD was **not measured**, n=0 (`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-dates-ws/DATE-VARIANCE-2026-09-09.md:3,65–72,84–95`).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:37:**Derived, conditional planning arithmetic.** For a paired log-contrast with crossed random effects,
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:43:Increasing seeds reduces the latter two terms; it cannot remove `σ_date²/D`. At D=1 the between-date component cannot be estimated from that panel. A date bootstrap repeatedly resamples the same date, so any resulting interval cannot support generalization across dates. That is the sound part of the wall. “More seeds cannot help at fixed D” is too strong; “more seeds cannot repair missing date replication” is correct.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:57:The approximation must not be promoted into the project's power result. Its variance must describe the **paired contrast**, not the raw EE spread of individual arms; common date shocks can cancel. For unequal-energy pooled ratios, the relevant variance is that of the pooled estimator's influence contributions, not automatically an unweighted average of datewise log ratios. The inspected merger correctly pools additive totals and applies the same product of date and seed resampling weights to both arms (`R/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/merge.py:178–183,272–343`). Separate worlds or many anchors on one date do not become independent dates. Temporal independence across archive dates also requires justification.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:85:The contract's coordinator instead receives a nominal model with **no realised fading** (`C/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:7`). Avoiding future-boundary feedback does not repair present realised-information access. These results can support an offline benchmark in that stronger information class. They do not establish attainable nominal-policy headroom, a nominal global ceiling, or deadline-compliant learned efficacy. **UNDETERMINED:** the corresponding nominal-only, fallback-inclusive contrast. It needs a receipt selected under the declared information and timing rules.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:97:**Verified, smoke receipt.** `R/.scratch/c3-panel-smoke-r8/smoke.json`, `screen_by_provisioning_rule.SEALED.contrasts.*.all_anchor`, contains eight contrasts taking four values. FULL versus ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL, DROP_C2, ONLY_C1 and ONLY_C3 all equal `-0.01745324091886997`. Each has `anchor_count: 1`; `smoke_test_not_evidence` is true; all eight learned `arm_owned_plans` have `proposal_repaired: true` and the same seed hash. The worker reports incomplete rule-specific construction and differing tape digests (`R/C3-PANEL-HARNESS-2026-09-10.md:11,70–92,123`).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:101:The ~+400% attribution also needs restraint. The opened smoke verifies **FULL versus external BASELINE = +401.714321%**, not an isolated head-independent argmax effect. Its inspected proposal-repair code ranks legal profiles by learned Q1+Q2 (`R/scripts/run_c3_panel_smoke.py:395–400`; `R/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/deployment.py:512–546`). Equal repaired seeds do not prove that this computation is head-independent. **UNDETERMINED:** the controller's particular +400% attribution to a separate exact-surplus one-shot step. A matching receipt with carrier, exact one-shot and learned endpoints, together with authenticated executable provenance, would settle it. The carrier comparison cannot establish route ownership in any event.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:105:Path 3 may be premature. The numerator correction restores a large full-buffer control-law contrast; SEALED coordination results already exceed 1%; the C1 input schema had repairable defects; some fitted models improve over the quoted head; actual paired date variance could be below 5%; and the archive contains many dates not yet evaluated. A sound learned-source experiment could therefore succeed without abandoning the original aspiration. The evidence cited above supports each possibility as a possibility.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:107:My response is that this defeats a verdict of *impossibility*, which I do not make. It does not establish the desired claim. The large effects change the action, reference, information class or intervention; the repaired learner has no reported decision result; actual variance is unmeasured; and the calibration and information mismatches remain. Retaining the aspiration as future work is compatible with changing what the present evidence is claimed to demonstrate. Selecting an unmeasured rescue as the adjudicated outcome would substitute hope for evidence.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:114:- **Path 2, enlarge the archive:** necessary if the eventual paired variance and practical margin demand it, but not sufficient. The open allocation decision precedes even exploiting the existing archive; independent new dates do not repair an intervention or calibration mismatch. Required archive size for the real experiment remains **UNDETERMINED**.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:117:These alternatives are not ruled out forever. They are ruled out as the present evidence-supported adjudication. The project cannot support its stated goal now; future feasibility remains **UNDETERMINED**, pending a conforming source intervention, repaired-head decision evidence, fresh-date allocation, measured paired variance, correct calibration, and the declared endpoint comparison.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:123:**Verified support and scope.** `B/.scratch/beamwidth/final-sealed-one-sided-1.66.json` and `B/.scratch/beamwidth/final-strict-one-sided-1.66.json`, `summary.pairings.correct.pooled_relative_ee_gain`, give `0.03618797702229193` and `0.008994207878970206`; `anchors[].tle_date` identifies 2026-05-30 and 2025-07-28. Reference, terminal search, information and horizon provenance are at `B/FINAL-BEAMWIDTH-CURVE-2026-09-10.md:21–25,101–109` and the code cited under Q2. The energy boundary comprises modeled user-link PA supply, per-beam chain circuitry, a common processing increment and specified idle states; it excludes spacecraft bus, other payload functions, feeder/ISL and terminal/ground energy (v1.8:7–8). No constellation-wide energy claim follows.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-rank-ws/STATIC-BASELINE-FAMILY-2026-09-10.md:9:Every arm uses `PANELCEIL`'s frozen global anchors 0–11 in declared order, the complete boundary-0 legal set (visible, D2-eligible, and cell-reachable), the `a-r0` corrected provisioning path, the anchor's declared prior-step incumbent, and singleton evaluation over all 48 realised boundaries. The reported numerator is saturated full-buffer successfully decoded forward-downlink information bits with **no demand cap**. Pooled EE is `sum(bits) / sum(joules)`, never a mean of anchor-local ratios.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-rank-ws/STATIC-BASELINE-FAMILY-2026-09-10.md:53:Each entry is `selection / end-to-end` seconds. End-to-end adds that arm's independent singleton 48-boundary committed evaluation. Tape construction (222.563 s, shared once by every arm) is excluded from arm timings. For the fixed point, selection includes its terminal certificate, exactly as in `PANELCEIL`.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/C3-PANEL-HARNESS-2026-09-10.md:72:For the smoke, each trained model runs the production Q1+Q2 proposal. Because all eight raw proposals failed the unchanged “served-user count must not decrease versus BASE” guard after only two smoke epochs, each ran the production deterministic repair against exact guarded support. Each then built its own `bounded-union-v2` catalogue around the repaired seed. The eight learned catalogues each had 911 rows; the external baseline catalogue had 1,004. The smoke happened to produce only two physical seed families—one learned family and BASELINE—so it is not evidence of the disjoint catalogues observed in the supporting audit. All nine authenticated scored-catalogue hashes were distinct.
