/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/PIPEAUDIT-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:79:**Verified — producer/consumer:** Training declaration:208–216 specifies the first 20 generated anchors, or the shorter available prefix. Runner:274–288 instead recursively discovers all JSONL files in `views`, or all staging views when no promoted directory exists. Runner:291–349 reads all of them and checks shared physics identity, not an exact anchor whitelist or equal C1/C2/C3 anchor support. Its CLI has neither a prefix/manifest option nor a resume option (Runner:581–606). Builder:354–359 publishes shard and sidecar separately; Builder:1042–1057 promotes individual shards and sidecars separately. The reader prefers `views` as soon as that directory exists, even during incomplete promotion.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/PIPEAUDIT-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:85:Required before launch: an immutable, complete shard inventory for each route and a separately bound evaluation-panel inventory, with explicit training overlap. Preserve those bytes for continuation and define which CLI restores which checkpoint. No filesystem snapshot or repair was made here.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/PIPEAUDIT-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:131:The strongest case is that the chain's numerical core already has substantial defensive plumbing: the real runner verifies canonical source views and sidecars, rejects missing C3 and mismatched physics, uses matched five-arm training, and reads checkpoints back through the sealed loader (Runner:217–270, 318–326, 541–563). The synthetic gate explicitly distinguishes four arm pairs; the [training receipt:94–107 and 124–134](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/TRAINING-RUNNER-2026-09-10.md:94) reports those checks and an epoch-100 KAT. The scorer reports a smoke exercising the five arms, knockout and all output tables, and candidly declares unavailable timing ([scorer receipt:29–34 and 69–108](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/DUAL-AXIS-SCORER-2026-09-10.md:29)). On that narrower claim, an authenticated complete corpus probably can produce readable checkpoints and formatted tables. That probability is an inference, not a test result from this audit.
