/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:7:The error in the first sentence has two independently checkable parts. Your [training gate, lines 14–17][gate] says an exact route marginal is an upper bound on a learned marginal, “strictly less whenever the head errs.” That is false in general. And `FULLSPAN`'s additive scorer is not the declared C1/C2 pair: it sums exact realised singleton changes over association **and power/mode controls**, then solves its own pooled surrogate ratio. Its full scorer optimizes realised outcomes with hindsight. Calling these “exact terms” does not make them exact implementations of your three heads.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:18:| 2 | `RESIDTOGGLE +5.62%` | Full exact pooled-EE optimization versus a singleton-additive surrogate optimizer, with a separate optimized price for each arm. Same expanded catalogue and realised service filter. | The maximum possible C3 source-training effect; a clean fixed-price residual toggle in the deployed pilot. |
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:26:**1. `FULLSPAN`: the headline is real for its experiment; your route attribution is not.** **V-code/V-receipt.** [FULLSPAN][fullspan] and [RESIDTOGGLE][toggle] specify the experiment. The [runner, lines 366–446][togglecode] evaluates candidates with `field="realised"`, all 48 boundaries, and constructs additive bits and energy as baseline plus the sum of complete-network singleton changes. There is no separate C2 forecast contribution in that construction. The catalogue includes association singletons, bundles, evacuations, adjacent-mode singletons, beam-wide controls, and joint association/control candidates.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:28:The declared C1 label instead contains a calibrated surplus and Phi; declared C2 consumes three offset projections. See [targets.py, lines 154–173][targets] and its `c2_persistence_forecast`. The pilot adds learned Q1 and Q2 differences in [its selector, lines 1524–1563][pilotselect]. Neither is the oracle singleton construction above. A 48-boundary immediate integral does not become the declared multi-step persistence target merely because both involve time.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:54:**D.** This error can scale with coalition size. If the joint and its `k` singletons use the snapshot but the reference uses the trajectory, define `delta = G(base,trajectory) − G(base,snapshot)`. Then `Psi_mixed = Psi_snapshot + (k−1)*delta`. A baseline discrepancy becomes a 99-fold residual discrepancy at a hundred-user coalition. Thus a very large “exact Ψ” can itself be an evaluator artefact; comparing learned and exact score ranges cannot diagnose model scaling until that identity is reconciled.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:85:The old spans and intervals remain descriptive evidence for their exact configurations. The thirty-date `+0.717% [0.436,0.997]` uses old pairing; the corrected twenty-anchor `+1.2913%` has **6/20**, not the **1/20** negatives printed in [STATUS, line 23][status]. The latest width comparison gives `+0.899421%`, **1/8** negative. You cannot attach one panel's interval to another panel's point estimate or transfer its variance unchanged after a policy change. The earlier `+5.888% [5.235,6.540]` interval belongs to the earlier provisioning condition.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:87:Your several-hundred-percent prefix gains are gains of the nonlearned search over geometry. They cannot become learned gains because a head is placed downstream. Conversely, the small increment of one bounded joint catalogue cannot cap all association improvement. “Mispaired” was too strong for an honestly paired joint extension of its own seed: that experiment estimates a valid conditional extension. Its defect was treating one traversal's endpoint as a canonical comparator.
