/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:107:**A. “The exact path repairs the data while preserving the inputs needed by a cheap predictor.” Wrong. V-code/V-receipt.** The [exact builder, lines 599–672][exactinputs] fills Q1 features from the candidate's evaluated margin, required power and ACM efficiency; Q2 features include evaluated future projections. [The cost receipt][rowcost] identifies those suppliers explicitly. The [data census][census] finds all Q1 and Q2 state vectors differ across the two paths at both diffed anchors. Switching paths changes features as well as labels, despite retaining the same dimensional schema. Some feature acquisition requires the very candidate solve the head is supposed to avoid. That may be allowed in an offline teacher; it is not free inference. The deployment feature supplier and its cost remain **UNDETERMINED** for the proposed successor.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:111:**C. “Missing contexts restrict C3 to changing about one fifth of catalogues/decisions.” Wrong as a frequency bound. V-code/D.** [Pilot lines 1509–1515][pilotcontexts] create contexts for every legal row with at least two changed users. The missing rows are the empty/singleton case under that rule. Their mutual scores cannot change, but **one** altered multi-user row can overtake every singleton at every anchor. A 79% row share gives no 21% bound on decision reachability. C3REACH's exact branch applies exact Ψ to **all** legal rows; the context gate is explicitly on the learned branch. A gate fork on an exact residual that is correctly zero for empty/singleton sets should be a no-op unless the factor changes something else.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:113:**D. “The residual sign is primarily a price-versus-context question.” Incomplete. V-code.** Learned versus exact additive background and mixed-horizon residual construction are missing from the declared causal story. The open-contradiction record also says a price explanation would be repairable “without touching any of the three routes.” That does not follow: C1 and Ψ are price-dependent targets. Changing eta changes labels, scale and potentially training, even if the architecture stays fixed.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:125:**J. “Predeclared means statistically unselected; unchanged numbers mean the estimand is unchanged.” Wrong. V-record/D.** The [requirement change][requirement] openly occurred after +5.62% was seen. The owner is entitled to change the goal. That creates an exploratory new claim and changes what success means, even if no number is recomputed. “Substantial” has no numerical decision rule, so G1 is not a determinate pass/fail test yet. Similarly, keeping the existing beam width because it was the “most stable point sampled” is an outcome-based justification for retention. Keeping a previously fixed value is defensible; claiming the exposure to favourable-antenna selection “disappears entirely” is not. Do not repair this by picking a fresh threshold from the same results.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:134:- A two-arrival occupancy-three witness is a pair interaction. The records repeatedly turn final occupancy three into a requirement for three changed users. Higher-order evidence must come from its own mixed differences/reversals.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:135:- A 32-pair block plus a summed omitted-pair residual preserves aggregate magnitude, not the identities of all omitted aggressors. “Nothing lost silently” must not become “full pairwise structure retained.”
