/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:164:| 2 | “SIGNFORK has resolved the residual contradiction.” | Hybrid learned/exact background and mixed-horizon Ψ remain even after a price×gate fork. The exact gate may be mathematically inert. | **20–40 min, no physics:** compare the two existing score-construction paths line by line; audit cached base/singleton/joint field and boundary identities, and whether a gate changes only empty/singleton zeros. Reconcile full/additive score identities before interpreting the fork. |
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:168:| 6 | “All certified endpoints are already optimized for the reported objective.” | Fixed-price, boundary-0 objective differs from capped 48-boundary pooled EE; two-swap failure is being generalized to singleton failure. | **10–30 min, existing receipts:** read certificate objective/horizon and the two capped swap rows. Before OBJMISMATCH arrives, write which neighbourhood its claim covers. Any zero result needs complete coverage, not just no improvement among sampled moves. |
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:179:A complete negative census establishes local optimality only on the tested legal singleton neighbourhood. A sampled negative result means “none found.” Neither excludes other starts, swaps or coordinated controls. Also distinguish per-anchor ratio optimization from whole-panel ratio optimization. With positive energy, a candidate improves the panel when `ΔN−eta_panel*ΔE>0`, where `eta_panel` is the current pooled ratio. Testing against each anchor's own eta answers a different question. A hindsight gain does not establish causal recoverability, C1 learnability, or that merely changing eta resolves the snapshot-versus-horizon mismatch.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:185:**EXACTGEN.** A pass means a specified set of rows faithfully implements a specified target and input contract, with authenticated source, fields, boundary grids, references, prices, Phi and three-offset semantics. It does not mean that a flag change alone repaired the deployed inference path. Require baseline/self-action identities and same-path base/singleton/joint construction; verify numerical units and the difference between exact arithmetic over binary64 receipts and exact physical truth. A zero algebraic identity residual cannot authenticate the semantics of its operands.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:187:Report row inclusion and coalition coverage, including empty/singleton handling, grand rows and missing sizes; legality filtering can change the training population. Separate target generation from inference-feature acquisition. For cost reconciliation, equal row counts do not imply equal work. If 49.03 and 632.83 seconds are reconciled by boundary count, optional coalition work or execution settings, state that mechanism and scope the rate accordingly. If not, cost is **UNDETERMINED**, not “affordable because one receipt says so.” Partial completion is an exact partial corpus, not a completed corpus. A complete corpus is readiness evidence, never EE evidence.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:195:**FACTORIAL.** Before any sign is read, require eight distinct **factor settings** `000…111`, plus the external nearest-eligible BASELINE as a ninth reference unless an explicit identity establishes coincidence. An exact `000` score may tie-break to a nonbaseline candidate; it is not automatically the trained all-neutral control. Distinguish exact factor removal from neutral-source retraining. Identify how C2 is represented: a genuine three-offset continuation, the sealed oracle tie-break, or an alternative partition of immediate singleton surplus. These are not interchangeable. Under the sealed oracle tie-break, zero C2 effect with a unique primary maximum is expected and is not evidence that learned Q2 cannot help proposals.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:13:The arithmetic against this convention remains severe. For a feasible uncapped fixed point, nominal SINR is approximately `Γ(n)`. At occupancy one, `Γ(1)` is the table floor, so `qΓ(1)` falls below every mode when the de-rating exceeds the negligible numerical clearance. The reported 9.16e−9 dB headroom cannot accommodate a 1.1–4.8 dB de-rating. The policy can therefore spend energy on a singleton while selecting no mode. Its universal singleton rejection need not have been anticipated merely because its constituent rules were deliberate.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:15:I tried to turn that pathology into a contradiction of radio physics; that attack fails. The occupancy comparison changes transmit power. A heavily occupied beam can receive much more power, including forced cap power when its target exceeds the table, and decode while the singleton does not. This is possible under the declared controller. Calling it “physically impossible” confuses a control policy with propagation at fixed power. Conversely, the claim that conservative mode selection “buys nothing” fails: demotion can buy decoding robustness at fixed power, until it runs out of modes.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:43:**A3. An outcome-selected correction-and-width pair — `CONSTRAINS_IT`; a bundled promotion of a favorable width is unsupported.**
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:74:| Exact label generation | 4,402 paired C1/C2 targets over five anchors took 591 s. Linear scaling to 180 anchors is approximately 5.9 serial wall-hours for these labels alone. |
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:90:There is a real service-counter discrepancy: scalar service uses AND across a user's transmissions within a boundary, while dense service uses OR. The ladder report discloses it. On the original matched eight anchors, scalar B/U/J counts are 301/778/789 and published dense counts 313/779/790. It changes the meaning of “served,” but not integrated bits or target attainment. The published positive-bit definition reproduces every receipt row. Preserve that definition for the comparison and disclose the discrepancy; do not silently repair the guard while changing provisioning.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:117:I also checked the counterfactual summaries. The 66.38% restoration is panel-wide; occupancy-one restoration after removing de-rating is 74.02%. The converged relaxed-cap control uses 100 W, rather than a literally absent cap; one configuration is invalid at 10⁹ W. The singleton failure survives the valid relaxed-cap control and the algebra, so those corrections do not rescue the old singleton policy. The quoted “cap from occupancy ten rather than twelve” is not universal: the Claude fixture binds at eleven rather than thirteen. Cap onset depends on geometry and coupling. The reported restoration differences should not be treated as a unique additive causal decomposition: interventions change coupled powers and their effects can overlap. [Counterfactual and fixture evidence](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/LADDER-CLAUDE-2026-09-10.md).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:121:If the change proceeds, preserve the original declared primary, seals, source, receipts, figures and unfavorable findings as results of the nominal-power convention, and explicitly state that the successor reverses v1.9's deliberate policy to pursue target-mode selection at the existing design percentile; disclose that all reported outcomes were known before this decision and make the rationale independent of C3's sign. Freeze the existing 1.66° one-sided beam width, constants, thresholds, signs, seeds, horizons, price, service guard and acceptance rules for the provisioning comparison; give any antenna change its own design decision, retain every already observed width as exploratory, and never promote a positive width to erase the original primary result. Specify and review the numerical clearance algorithm at every affected scalar and dense site, then regenerate all affected power/interference solves, search paths, catalogues, service and rate metrics, EE figures, calibration diagnostics at the frozen price, features, labels, learned models, trajectories, contrasts, intervals and admission decisions before carrying them into successor claims; reuse only demonstrably unaffected exogenous inputs and controls. Publish both rules, all widths, energy costs, user losses, caps, failures and negative signs, including the simple-versus-strict numerical distinction, and report the current full-width strict comparison as uncompleted until it exists. Disclose the shared commissioning and assumptions of the reviews, the nominal/full-buffer service semantics, the scalar/dense service discrepancy, repeated-observation denominators, TRAIN-only panels and bounded-search limitations; claim neither 90% network availability nor guaranteed target delivery from the quantile identity. Any later confirmation must follow a prospectively frozen protocol on the reserved unused confirmation data, with unchanged acceptance criteria and failures reported in full.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-fable-ws/DECOMP-fable-2026-09-10.md:1:**Yes, conditionally: under the corrected argmax-over-catalogue selector the residual's obstruction is not reachability (c) but conditioning (b), and a decomposition by physical term — credited bits under the candidate's occupancy, resource energy under the candidate's activation, and continuation — is three separately ablatable information sources, is well conditioned on the same exact numbers (parts-to-total 1.00–1.61x against 1.57–22.99x for the residual split), and is nonzero on singleton rows so every route can flip the argmax in the pilot selector and fire the first move in the panel harness; but it is a declared v2 of the route identities rather than the residual, it forfeits "coordination" as a separately ablatable route, and whether each route is individually *substantial* for pooled EE cannot be settled on paper.**
