/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-fable-ws/DECOMP-fable-2026-09-10.md:39:Of the three candidate causes the controller lists, "`contexts.get` returns None for most rows" is verified true **and is not a defect**: in the pilot, contexts are built only for rows with ≥ 2 changed users (`:1508-1512`); the sealed bounded catalogue is base + every legal unilateral + 2 S0-proposals + ≤ 180 pairwise rows + one evacuation per active beam (`_catalogue_with_census`). From the r8 plan (911 rows, 701 nominal rank evaluations = base + 700 unilaterals) about **211 rows (23%) are multi-user**; the other 77% get no context by design (contract §C2 hard-zero anchor). So under S-cat the residual can re-rank about a quarter of the catalogue and can never reorder singleton rows among themselves.
