/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/DECOMP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:125:It is not a pointwise improvement theorem for the measured anchor. The 22.9853 figure is pointwise; 1.73205 is a population RMS bound under strong forecasting assumptions. Individual innovations can still nearly cancel on a particular row pair, estimated heads need not be orthogonal, and relative errors of the stipulated size are not guaranteed. Winner selection also conditions on an extreme among many rows; fixed-pair RMS control alone does not control that maximum or guarantee the argmax. I cannot infer new route values, or a new condition number for the 40.034 example, from the supplied totals.
