/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/DECOMP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:139:These are existence proofs of a channel. They do not show that this catalogue has a suitable pair for every route, that those routes contain unique information, or that the switched commit improves reporting EE.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/DECOMP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:145:If route names must retain their literal declared targets, C1 and C3 retain the measured cancellation by definition. If temporal inputs are determined by local/common geometry, their innovation is identically zero. If resource information is already in mandatory coordinator inputs, calling it a new source creates no unique information. If all admissible source effects are row-constant, no argmax changes. Even nonzero effects may be redundant, so FULL need not improve over every pair. Better prediction of boundary-0 F may have no positive effect on pooled 48-boundary EE. A single masked complete-score predictor with three input blocks could also fail the owner's intended meaning of three learned routes unless the policy change is expressly declared.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/DECOMP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:147:These are serious objections. For a particular authenticated information partition, `Q_J = Q_(J without {r})` almost surely would prove that source has no incremental Bayes forecasting contribution. For a fixed implemented scorer, identical rankings and identical downstream execution would prove no committed effect on that panel. If the original numerical targets cannot change, their residual is algebraically unique and its observed conditioning cannot be repaired by renaming.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/DECOMP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:157:Headroom is not a budget of three independent gains. Routes may exploit the same configurations. Conversely, the stated ordering does not imply that three singleton percentage improvements must add arithmetically, so a small total gap is not by itself an impossibility proof. The oracle mode result is also not evidence of three sources and cannot be inserted into the decision-time inputs. Its causal measurement remains pending.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/DECOMP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:175:3. **Measure conditioning on the fixed full catalogue.** Retain exact and predicted row scores and pairwise margins, route increments, absolute errors, error covariance, zero/near-zero margins, ties, winning gaps and argmax agreement. Report component-to-net ratios separately for rows and relevant row pairs. For the innovation candidate, report L2 orthogonality departures and errors of each conditional forecast, as well as the actual winning-margin behaviour. Do not call a lower RMS loss, a changed normalisation, or a small average error a successful EE contribution. If operational errors still arise from comparable cancellation and ranking instability, the claimed practical conditioning improvement is unsupported even if the population theorem remains true.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/DECOMP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:179:5. **Evaluate precisely the owner's contrasts under the existing reporting protocol.** Let P0 be the declared reference baseline and P_J the explicitly specified policy with active sources J. ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL remains P_empty under its own name; it is never relabelled P0. If “baseline plus route” is a different policy wrapper from a factorial singleton, that wrapper must be specified and measured explicitly. Compute EE as pooled capped committed bits divided by pooled committed joules over the 48 boundaries, with the sealed energy accounting, scoring and guard. Report each singleton's gain over P0, FULL against each pair, and every pair against ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL, plus matched source contrasts and commit differences. Treat the two provisioning rules separately according to their existing status; do not choose the favourable one after inspection.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/DECOMP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:181:6. **Respect the actual checkpoint and experiment inventory.** The five-arm format covers FULL, the three pairs represented by DROP arms, and ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL. It does not supply the three singleton policies. The complete eight-subset claim therefore cannot be established from that five-arm inventory alone. Do not request an eight-arm sealed checkpoint or extend epochs to 3,000/9,000. Singleton evidence needs an explicitly declared evaluation/ablation extension with valid provenance, or an explicitly declared format change; neither is silently authorised by this design answer. Recomputed masked forecasts are not automatically equivalent to separately trained source-neutral arms. Five arms, 2,000 epochs and cadence 100 establish feasibility for the existing format only. No new training is proposed here.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/DECOMP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:183:For the stated endpoint requirement, a nonpositive singleton gain, FULL failing to exceed a pair, or a pair failing to exceed ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL rejects that ordering for the evaluated design and panel, subject to the existing inference rules. About 1% singleton gains do not meet the owner's stated materiality requirement. No exact materiality threshold beyond that exclusion was supplied; use an already authorised definition if present, otherwise report effect sizes and leave borderline materiality unresolved. I will not invent a new threshold or scientific gate. Unchanged commits with matched accounting establish zero contribution on those cases. Passing source or conditioning diagnostics cannot replace passing the EE requirement.
