The off-axis lead has resolved more narrowly than the initial clue suggested: V0.25’s physics already multiplies the path by `transmit_gain_linear(direct_angles)`, so it does not share the sibling’s “beams are physically channel-identical” defect. The sealed v1 learner row did contain a zero angle placeholder, but Q1 v2 already repairs that row feature, and Q1 v3 adds the exact nominal-gain scalar. The remaining question is therefore representation/target use—not missing off-axis physics—and I’m preserving that distinction in the report.
