    31	7. the same physical link sustainable for at least two consecutive slots;
    32	8. θ actually traversing the frozen gain curve.
    33	
    34	Items 1, 5, 6, and 8 are **[grounded]** by the 100-UE gate
    35	(`100UE-GEOMETRY-PASS`, ADR-008 UE-scale amendment). Items 2, 3, 4, and 7 are
    36	what this ADR tested against the production adapter.
    37	
    38	## Measurement
    39	
    40	The probe uses the **existing production Family-B adapter** with nothing
    41	relaxed: Walker `180/9/1` at `53°`, `780 km`, rotating-ECEF propagation mapped
    42	into the declared ECI fixture, the pre-existing `40° N / 116° E` service-area
    43	centre, body-fixed LVLH nadir plus six ring beams at `ring_tilt_deg = 2.0`, the
    44	frozen `3.32°` full HPBW, the candidate rule `off-axis ≤ full HPBW and
    45	elevation ≥ 0°`, and the three-active-beam ceiling.
    46	
    47	Two fixed service areas were scanned over a full 24 h support. A 5 s coarse
    48	sweep flagged every pass whose nearest sub-satellite point came within 300 km
    49	of the area centre, and each flagged pass was refined to 1 s slots, clipped to
    50	the declared support — 23,420 refined slots in total. Every user's nearest
    51	geometric candidate is then put through the declared three-active-beam
    52	admission, so coverage and dwell are reported both before admission
    53	(*candidate*) and after it (*served*); only the served view feeds a gate.
    54	
    55	Producer: `scripts/run_moving_footprint_production_geometry_probe.py`.
    56	Artifact: `.scratch/moving-footprint-production-geometry-20260820/production-geometry-probe-24h-v2.json`
    57	(SHA-256 `bcbbc274fc91eaaa2fe76071e46835db0dfcea53dd446e73590d16738b999d70`).
    58	The superseded pre-review artifact `…-24h.json` (`43301ce9…`) is retained
    59	unmodified for provenance.
