# Sibling concept transfer audit — 2026-09-10

## Scope, evidence rules, and the filter

This is a records assessment, not an experiment. No checkpoint, training job, simulation, or physics computation was read or run. The enumeration boundary is every materially distinct idea in the supplied sibling records that changes the physical contract, observation, objective, training signal, action selection, or deployment boundary. Pure governance devices (hash fences, preregistration, seed rules, artifact catalogs, and statistical reporting conventions) are not counted as design concepts. ADR-001 through ADR-009 are nevertheless covered explicitly because the request names them; where an ADR is process-only, it is enumerated and rejected as such.

Evidence tags used below:

- **[V] verified by reading the record**: directly stated in the cited sibling file, or stated in the owner-supplied current-project facts and cited there as such.
- **[D] derived**: a necessary comparison or consequence of two verified statements.
- **[I] inferred**: a plausible transfer mechanism that would still need a project-local test.

The current-project facts F1–F9 are accepted as **[V-owner]** because they were supplied as today’s verified panel. They were not recomputed here. In short: F1 concentration is EE-optimal; F2 the optimization objective and pooled EE disagree; F3 the action is user-relative and does not suffer the sibling’s slot-to-physical collapse; F4 there is no hard beam-user cap; F5 the interaction route reaches the decision as one scalar against about 100 per-user terms; F6 98.13% of the catalog has set size at most two; F7 a joint profile beats the best per-user rule by 10.78%; F8 Q1/Q2 v2 omit `nominal_gain` and cannot express `RSS_MAX`; F9 the sealed head loses to linear calibration on all three routes.

The four required historical labels are quoted exactly. Full-DQfD is classified **“tried and failed”** only on the historical load-only contract whose measurements were actually adjudicated; the later corrected-physics record explicitly invalidates that result for current-physics claims. Its margin-off control remains **“shelved untested.”**

## Part 1 and Part 2 — complete concept inventory and nine-fact filter

