|---:|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Separate Python reproduction plus later artifact bridge (ADR-001) | Isolate a paper-faithful trainer from platform/UI assumptions, then bridge artifacts later. | **“demonstrated to work”** as an engineering boundary; ADR status is `Accepted`. [`ADR-001...md:9-24`](ref/docs/ADR-001-separate-python-reproduction-project.md#L9), [`:56-61`](ref/docs/ADR-001-separate-python-reproduction-project.md#L56) | none | reject |
| 2 | Three per-objective Q heads plus fixed linear scalarization (baseline MODQN) | Preserve throughput, handover, and load objectives in separate value heads, then rank actions by a weighted sum. | **“demonstrated to work”** as a faithful reproduction surface, not as an advantage claim. [`PROJECT...md:98-99`](ref/docs/PROJECT-STATE-AND-FAILURE-LEDGER.md#L98), [`:212-228`](ref/docs/PROJECT-STATE-AND-FAILURE-LEDGER.md#L212) | none: F2 is evidence that the existing scalarized objective is the problem, not that more of the same fixes it | reject |
| 3 | Additive instantaneous system-EE reward plus ratio-of-sums evaluation | Give every per-user transition an additive contribution `R_u/P_sys` whose sum equals instantaneous system EE, while reporting total bits / total energy across time rather than a mean of instantaneous ratios. | **“demonstrated to work”** for algebraic/runtime closure; effectiveness was not established and ADR-003 is now archived. [`ADR-003...md:132-173`](ref/docs/ADR-003-canonical-ee-closure.md#L132) | **F1, F2** | **survives** |
