    79	**[V-sibling]** The sibling’s pre-2026-06-04 base channel computed no off-axis transmit-gain term, so every beam on a satellite was throughput-identical for a user. Its own record says this confounded `NO_A4_ADVANTAGE` and the “collapse is reward-optimal” story (`ref/docs/failure-route-ledger.md:13-28`; `ref/docs/research/catfish-faithful-route-a/08-converged-faithful-baseline-foundation-sdd.md:34-68`). The repaired sibling channel computed per-user/per-beam angle, applied `G_T(theta)`, and became position-dependent/QoS-live. That is a physical-channel repair.
    80	
    81	**[V-current record]** V0.25’s provider instead computes `direct_angles`, applies `transmit_gain_linear(direct_angles) * direct_path` to form `nominal_gain`, and returns that derived gain (`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/provider_legacy.py:717-725,939`). The batch evaluator consumes the angle-derived nominal gain directly (`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/batch.py:203`). Therefore the physical panel did not flatten all options to boresight.
