   126	- **Why it transfers:** the algebraic identity `sum_u r_u = system EE` and ratio-of-sums reporting do not depend on the sibling’s channel numbers. The physics provider supplies rate and power; the closure governs how they enter learning and evaluation.
   127	- **Sealed-inventory change:** replace or add an objective route whose per-user terms add to the same pooled system EE used for judgment; keep exact-`F` as a diagnostic until order equivalence is demonstrated. Do not add fairness/spread pressure merely because the sibling did.
   128	- **Cost:** medium. It touches reward definition, calibration, checkpoint selection semantics, and every consumer of the objective, so it requires a new versioned route even though the formula is simple.
   129	
   130	### 2. Add RSS_MAX demonstrations with a DQfD-style ranking loss—only on Q1 v3 or later
   131	
   132	- **Binding released:** F8.
   133	- **Why it transfers:** the demonstrator is project-local and already measured; only the mechanism transfers. The sibling’s data and physics are irrelevant.
   134	- **Sealed-inventory change:** a demonstration dataset carrying the same sealed features plus RSS_MAX action labels; a demo-aware replay partition; Q-scale-aware large-margin ranking on demonstration rows; optional pretraining; and an explicit margin-free demo-TD control. The Q1 v3 nominal-gain feature stays—DQfD does not replace it.
   135	- **Cost:** medium. Data production is cheap, but loss scaling, action-mask parity, leakage control, and the F7 demonstrator ceiling require careful preregistration. The sibling bundle was **tried and failed** on an obsolete load-only contract; that result is a caution, not a current-physics veto.
   136	
   137	### 3. Add a joint-profile construction route, preferably deterministic before learned
   138	
   139	- **Binding released:** F5 and F7; F6 makes exact/local combinatorial construction unusually tractable.
   140	- **Why it transfers:** F7 is project-local proof that independent rules leave 10.78% on the table. Joint optimization addresses the decision factorization, not a satellite propagation constant.
   141	- **Sealed-inventory change:** retain the per-user scores but add a profile-level consumer that evaluates/constructs assignments jointly. Start with the already-demonstrated non-learned auction/assignment family as a diagnostic ceiling; a learned coordination decoder is a separate, higher-cost hypothesis and inherits the sibling’s reachability failure.
   142	- **Cost:** medium for a deterministic bounded-catalog solver; high for a learned decoder. It also changes the deployment boundary, so it is disallowed if pure per-user argmax is a project requirement.
   143	
   144	### 4. Replace the single interaction scalar with per-option congestion context
   145	
   146	- **Binding released:** F5.
   147	- **Why it transfers:** the exact congestion equation differs, but the structural issue does not: a scalar added once cannot represent which candidate option caused which occupancy-dependent spectral-efficiency/power consequence. The sibling’s `χ` pattern is an example of pre-action, option-indexed context rather than a transferable numerical feature set.
   148	- **Sealed-inventory change:** add option-aligned occupancy/load context at the same boundary as Q1 v3’s nominal gain. Do **not** import the sibling’s cap-specific “competitor rank” blindly; derive only fields supported by this project’s `required_se(rate, occupancy)` and 1.65 W cap.
   149	- **Cost:** medium. The representation and linear-calibration tests change, but no new optimizer or deployment coordinator is required.
   150	
   151	## Rejection ledger — one line each
   152	
   153	The following one-line ledger is intentionally repetitive: it is the durable “do not rerun the fishing trip” output.
   154	
   155	1. **Separate reproduction/artifact bridge:** useful project hygiene, but it releases none of F1–F9.
   156	2. **Three-head fixed scalarization:** already implicated by F2; more head separation does not align the objective with pooled EE.
   157	3. **κ per-user EE allocation:** sibling algebra found a reverse incentive; it is a worse surrogate, not a repair.
   158	4. **Angle-aware EE as a reward variant:** rejected separately from the missing-information fix; changing reward cannot recover a feature that is absent/zero.
   159	5. **Proportional-fair angle-aware EE:** imposes spread/fairness pressure against F1’s monotone concentration result.
   160	6. **Handover-aware EE:** no present fact identifies a missing handover term as binding.
   161	7. **Active-TX/QoS hysteresis:** sibling failure was coordination noise; no matching present symptom exists.
   162	8. **PopArt:** failed there and F9 points toward simpler level calibration, not adaptive target normalization.
   163	9. **Reward reweighting/non-EE reward:** does not repair the measured exact-`F`/pooled-EE order mismatch.
   164	10. **Action masking:** current actions are user-relative and already span many physical beams (F3).
   165	11. **Hard capacity cap/greedy admission:** this project has no such cap (F4).
   166	12. **Capacity-weight sweep:** same missing premise as the hard-cap route, plus F1 favors concentration.
   167	13. **Earth-fixed realistic cells:** imports a geometry regime; only the off-axis information-integrity lesson transfers.
   168	14. **Holistic environment rebuild:** this project already has full-service panel measurements; no whole-environment degeneracy is established.
   169	15. **Unreachable-offset masking:** no current saturation or unreachable-slot defect is measured, and F3 distinguishes the encoding.
   170	16. **HOBS interference:** sibling audit showed the lever can reward collapse; current F1 already settles the relevant direction.
   171	17. **Frequency-sub-band coupling:** its sibling “win” was a throughput artifact/corner rule and no analogous coupling exists here.
   172	18. **Learned coordination decoder:** dominated as a first step by the deterministic joint-profile route; sibling forward reachability remained unresolved.
   173	19. **QMIX/VDN:** value mixing without joint action construction does not release F7.
   174	20. **M1 experience stratification:** selecting high-reward replay does not make missing nominal gain expressible.
   175	21. **M2 asymmetric discount:** structural dead weight in the sibling and no present horizon binding is measured.
   176	22. **M3 random intervention:** a replay schedule without the missing feature/ranking target does not address F8.
   177	23. **ACRM:** never enabled there and addresses challenger competition, not any current measured binding.
   178	24. **Source-faithful DFT/WMMSE Phase-I:** wrong action/physics semantics and never assembled even in the sibling.
   179	25. **LEO-native immutable prefill pipeline:** excellent provenance discipline, but RSS_MAX source quality is already known; the missing piece is representation/loss.
   180	26. **Margin-free demo TD:** retain only as DQfD’s control; sibling evidence says it can leave unshown discrete actions unanchored.
   181	27. **BC k-NN:** the project can deploy RSS_MAX directly, so a clone adds correlated-error/generalization cost without releasing a new binding.
   182	28. **Live cross-user z-score:** solved a sibling common-mode collapse absent under F3 and introduces an avoidable cross-user dependency.
   183	29. **Frozen-z:** never existed in the sibling training config and no current input-scale defect is measured.
   184	30. **Differentiable capacity penalty:** genuinely ran, but its premise is absent under F4 and its form does not penalize concentration anyway.
   185	31. **Coordinator coalition replay:** retired before training and is a less direct route to F7 than deterministic joint construction.
   186	32. **Per-objective three-Catfish/admission banks:** target-starvation is not the measured reason exact `F` disagrees with pooled EE.
   187	33. **Measurement-triggered directional intervention:** sophisticated scheduling around an unmeasured stagnation problem.
   188	34. **Continuous system-level actor:** jointness is relevant, but continuous RIS/beamforming action semantics do not match the 98.13% singleton/pair catalog.
   189	35. **Previous-step angle-power recurrence/moving footprint:** different physics; retain only the information-closure lesson already ranked #1.
   190	36. **Dynamic demand/queues:** no current fact establishes traffic dynamics as binding.
   191	37. **DRQN:** no current fact establishes partial observability or missing temporal memory as binding.
   192	38. **Preference-conditioned MORL:** F2 is a metric-definition mismatch, not missing preference coverage.
   193	
   194	## Bottom line
   195	
   196	**[D]** The sibling’s most valuable transfer is a negative discipline: do not import its anti-collapse agenda. F1, F3, and F4 remove the premises behind most of its catalog. The live shortlist instead follows this project’s own evidence: align the learned objective with the judged pooled metric; use the project-local RSS_MAX demonstrator only after its feature is present; and only then pay for joint action construction or richer interaction context.
   197	
   198	**[I]** If pure per-user deployment is a hard constraint, the joint-profile concept is diagnostic-only. That boundary can reduce the actionable list from four to three; it does not revive any rejected sibling route. The off-axis lead is already closed as “related historical observation defect, not shared active physical defect.”

